{
  "about": [
    "MSFP Media version 0's base (spec/v0/base.md): text encodings (section 2.1), JSON (section 2.2), language tags (section 2.4) and open values (section 3). Sections named alone are base's. Generated by tools/vectors.",
    "base64url: a value (text) of a field whose value is bytes bytes long, as section 2.1 judges it: only A-Z a-z 0-9 - _, no padding, no white space, the length the bytes fix (43 characters for 32, 22 for 16, 86 for 64), the unused bits of the last character zero. hex: lowercase 0-9 a-f only, at least one character. decimals: decimal integers written as text, outside JSON: 0 or [1-9][0-9]*, no sign, no white space, at most 2^53 - 1.",
    "json: bodies (text, or hex when it isn't printable ASCII) as section 2.2 judges them: valid when they are I-JSON (RFC 7493) in a JSON text (RFC 8259) and a JSON object at the top, nest no value deeper than level 64 (the body's object at level 0, a member's value or an array's entry one level deeper than what holds it), and hold no number whose magnitude rounds above the largest IEEE 754 double (a number too small for one counts as 0): UTF-8 without a byte order mark, no surrogate code points and no noncharacters, escaped or not, no object with the same member name twice once escapes are decoded, JSON white space only (space, tab, line feed, carriage return) between tokens. A number with a fraction or an exponent, -0 and null are valid here: what a member takes is its field's (integers; null is no valid value of any member). integers: a number's text as it appears in a body, where an integer is expected: no fraction, no exponent, not -0, from -(2^53 - 1) to 2^53 - 1.",
    "languageCodes: a media server's language code (text) and the tag a source sends for it (output), or none (valid false): an ISO 639-2 code, /B or /T, of a language with an ISO 639-1 code sent as that code, the rest kept, in BCP 47's case conventions; und, mul, zxx and mis not sent (sections 2.4 and 2.3).",
    "openTokens: values of open fields (section 3). A token is 1 to 32 characters of a-z 0-9 . _ -. In a fact (titles, play's answer) a token is kept as it is, known or not (valid true), never turned into another value; a value that isn't a token is malformed (valid false): dropped alone when the member is optional, with the entry holding it (a copy, a track, an extra) when the member is required. In a request, an unknown token is ignored where the field is a hint and refused where it names what to serve: 409 delivery-refused for a delivery, 409 target-refused for a target (a remux's media type, a transcode codec, a range; playing sections 2.1, 2.2 and 2.7); only a value that isn't a token gets 400.",
    "openMediaTypes: values of media-type fields (section 3): an IANA-form media type, lowercase, exactly one /, no parameters, each half starting with a letter or a digit, at most 127 characters of a-z 0-9 . + - _ /. Kept as it is, known or not (valid true); otherwise malformed (valid false), handled as openTokens says. Libraries and titles carry no kind (listing sections 2 and 3): a kind member is unknown, ignored; kind is a filter of the titles request (titleRequests in listing.json)."
  ],
